<template id="request_dialog"><h2>Request Adjustable walking cane</h2><p>Next, provide your identity and address evidence. If you are requesting as a caregiver, provide your own evidence.</p><p>Your request is sent to the donor only after verification succeeds and you confirm submission. The donor will then see your verified name and ZIP code and decide to approve or decline your request.</p><p>This step does not reserve or hold the item.</p><button class="primary" data-action="begin-evidence" data-id="2">Continue to identity verification</button></template>
<template id="identity_dialog"><h2>Verify identity for your request</h2><p>Adjustable walking cane</p><p>You selected Request this item. Your request has not been sent to the donor. Complete identity and address verification first; failed verification will not create a pending donor request.</p><form id="request-form" data-id="2"><label>I’m requesting for<select name="for"><option value="self">Myself</option><option value="caregiver">Someone I’m helping</option></select></label><section class="note"><h3>Identity and address evidence</h3><p>Please upload a utility bill or a government issued id showing your name and address to verify your identity and location. If you are a caregiver, provide your own evidence, not the care recipient’s.</p><p><b>Design simulation only:</b> choose a fictional image below. No real file is uploaded, no OCR service runs, and no backend database is connected.</p><label>Sample document image<select name="document"><option value="utility">Fictional utility bill</option><option value="license">Fictional driver’s license</option><option value="blurred">Unreadable image / missing ZIP</option><option value="failure">Simulate processing failure</option></select></label><button class="" data-action="extract-evidence" data-id="">Simulate upload & extract details</button><div id="evidence-preview" aria-live="polite"></div></section><label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="disclose" required> <span>I consent to share my verified name and ZIP code with <b>Jordan</b> for this request for <b>Adjustable walking cane</b>. If I am a caregiver, these are my own details. The document image is not shared.</span></label><div class="note"><b>Meet safely, together.</b><br>Arrange pickup or return in a public, nonresidential place, in daylight while the venue is open. FreeDME does not inspect equipment, arrange transport or guarantee returns. Decline an item that seems unsafe or unsuitable.</div><label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="ack" required> <span>I understand pickup is my responsibility and have read the equipment and safety guidance (preview v0.9).</span></label><label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="authority" required> <span>If helping someone else, I have authority to act for them and understand whose information would be disclosed.</span></label><p class="error-text" id="request-error" role="alert"></p><button class="primary">Send verified request to donor</button></form></template>
<template id="question_dialog"><h2>Ask A Question</h2><p>About Adjustable walking cane</p><form id="item-question" data-item="2"><label>Your question<textarea name="question" required maxlength="500" rows="5" placeholder="Ask about dimensions, condition or features. Use fictional details only."></textarea></label><p class="muted">Do not include phone numbers, addresses or medical details. A simulated SMS will notify the donor; no real text is sent.</p><button class="primary">Submit question</button></form></template>
<template id="approval_dialog"><h2>Approve request</h2><p>Folding walker</p><p>Optionally suggest a handoff day, time and public location. The recipient still needs to accept your offer and agree on the arrangements.</p><form id="approve-request" data-id="R-101"><label>Suggested day<input type="date" name="day" min="2026-10-16"></label><label>Suggested time (Pacific Time)<input type="time" name="time"></label><label>Suggested public meeting location<input name="place" maxlength="200" placeholder="For example, the library main entrance"></label><p class="muted">Choose a public, nonresidential place in daylight while it is open. Suggestions appear only in this exchange; no location or time is included in the SMS preview.</p><p role="alert" class="error-text"></p><button class="primary">Approve</button></form></template>
<template id="answer_dialog"><h2>Answer question</h2><h3>Adjustable walking cane</h3><p data-design-style="s17"><strong>Question:</strong> Is the height adjustable?</p><form id="question-answer" data-question="Q1"><label>Your answer<textarea name="answer" required maxlength="1000" rows="5"></textarea></label><p>Use fictional details only. Do not include private contact, address or medical details. The recipient receives a simulated SMS notification; no real text is sent.</p><button class="primary">Submit answer</button></form></template>
<template id="review_dialog"><h2>Review Walker awaiting review</h2><p>Wheel condition needs clarification. Model: Unknown.</p><form id="review" data-id="7"><label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="disclosures" required> <span>I reviewed the sample disclosures, photos and category configuration.</span></label><label>Recall screening result<select name="recall" required><option value="">Select outcome</option><option value="no_match">No match found (sample)</option><option value="potential">Potential match</option><option value="confirmed">Confirmed unresolved recall</option><option value="insufficient">Insufficient identification</option></select></label><label>Review source<input name="source" required placeholder="Sample FDA / CPSC / manufacturer review"></label><label>Decision reason<textarea name="reason" required placeholder="Explain the outcome to the donor"></textarea></label><label>Decision<select name="decision"><option value="available">Approve for publication</option><option value="pending_review">Request corrections</option><option value="rejected">Reject</option></select></label><label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="resolved" > <span>The sample identification / safety hold has been resolved through documented review.</span></label><p class="error-text" id="review-error" role="alert"></p><button class="primary">Record review</button><p><small>Sample screening only, not a recall check or equipment certification.</small></p></form></template>
<template id="share_dialog"><h2 class="modal-title">Spread the word</h2><p>Copy a draft, personalize it, and send it from your own app. Nothing is sent by FreeDME.</p><p class="note">Design preview: confirm the public website is ready before inviting others.</p><label for="share-text">Text message</label><textarea id="share-text" readonly rows="5">Help a neighbor. Give equipment a new life! FreeDME connects neighbors offering free permanent giveaways or short-term loans of gently used mobility equipment. Give, lend, receive or borrow—and keep useful equipment in use. Learn more: https://freedme.org</textarea><label for="share-subject">Email subject</label><input id="share-subject" readonly value="Help a neighbor. Give equipment a new life — meet FreeDME"><label for="share-email">Email message</label><textarea id="share-email" readonly rows="10">Hi,

I thought you might like to know about FreeDME, a Bay Area community nonprofit initiative with two connected goals: neighbors helping neighbors and responsible reuse of mobility equipment.

ME connects people offering gently used mobility equipment as a free permanent giveaway or a free short-term loan with neighbors who genuinely need it. The owner chooses whether to give or lend; every listing shows the type, city and neighborhood, and the maximum duration for a loan.

An item you no longer need, or can spare for a while, may help someone else. Giving, lending, receiving and borrowing can keep suitable equipment in use.

The proposed pilot focuses on canes, matching standard underarm crutches, standard walkers, adult rollators, standard adult manual wheelchairs and adult transport chairs.

Have equipment to give or lend? Looking for an item? Know someone who might benefit? Learn more at:
https://freedme.org

Participants arrange pickup and any return directly at a public, nonresidential place in daylight while open. The owner decides whether to accept a request. A lender keeps ownership. Returns and extensions are between the two parties; FreeDME does not guarantee or recover equipment or resolve private loan disputes. FreeDME does not inspect equipment or provide delivery. Reuse does not override condition, fit or safety requirements.

Please share this with friends, family or neighbors who may find it useful.

Thank you!</textarea></template>
